{"name":"Petrol Slumber","hex":"#243640","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"petrol","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fluid consisting of a mixture of refined petroleum hydrocarbons, primarily consisting of octane, commonly used as a motor fuel.","A motor vehicle powered by petrol (as opposed to diesel)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fill or supply (a vehicle, etc.) with petrol."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/petrol"},{"term":"slumber","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very light state of sleep, almost awake.\n\n A very heavy state of sleep.","A very heavy state of sleep."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be in a very light state of sleep, almost awake.","To be inactive or negligent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slumber"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gasoline","blocks":[{"text":"Gasoline or petrol is a petrochemical product, a transparent, yellowish and flammable liquid normally used as a fuel for spark-ignited internal combustion engines. It is chemically composed of organic compounds derived from the fractional distillation of petroleum and later chemically enhanced with gasoline additives. It is a high-volume profitable product produced in crude oil refineries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Gasoline_in_mason_jar.jpg/330px-Gasoline_in_mason_jar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gasoline","wikidata":"Q39558"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/GasolineComp.png/500px-GasolineComp.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/GasolineComp.png/1280px-GasolineComp.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/GasolineComp.png/500px-Gasoli